{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 111, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "With edge 4 empty, a conv on edge 5 becomes one of the few or only learned paths into the output node, so adding it helps far more (rows 3-4 vs 1-2)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "In a skip-dominated cell, another skip on edge 3 brings no learned transformation and further weakens the cell (row 17 strongly negative, while conv parents gain)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an empty input-to-output edge adds a new path, whereas replacing an existing skip loses the residual shortcut (rows 87, 90 vs 86)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 5 is empty, edge 4's conv carries most of the learned signal to the output, so swapping it for pooling hurts more (rows 39-40 vs 31, 33)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Pooling on an empty edge adds an extra aggregation path, while pooling in place of a conv loses learned capacity (rows 34, 36, 38 vs 31, 32, 37)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv where there was no edge gains much more than swapping a conv or skip for it (rows 71-79 vs 76, 77, 80)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "In a cell otherwise made of parameter-free pooling, the first conv supplies most of the cell's learning capacity (row 30 gains about 48pp vs about 1-3pp in conv cells)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting a conv on the edge into the output loses more than deleting a skip or pool there (rows 61-64, 68-70 vs 65-66)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 4 is empty, removing edge 3 can leave the output with almost nothing feeding it, which collapses the network (row 83 vs 81-82)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Pruning edge 1 hurts mainly when it carried a 3x3 conv, not when it carried a skip or pool (rows 41, 42, 48-50 vs 44-45)."}], "tok": 33084, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "none", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "none", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_